    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (74.41) and **Lawrence Butler** (70.88) headline our lineup as the premier offensive anchors. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** draws a favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a, benefiting from a significant SP skill advantage (+10%) and the stability of the #3 hole. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** is poised for a breakout performance against Bradley; he benefits from a massive 10% park boost and a +13% platoon edge, making him a high-upside play to chase both power and counting stats. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) also warrants specific mention as a high-value start, as his +12% dynamic platoon edge against Jobe pushes him well into the \"Strong\" start tier, validating our continued faith in his role at 1B.\n\nStrategic optimization favored high-ceiling matchups, leaving **Gleyber Torres** (50.33) as our most difficult bench decision. Despite a favorable +10% boost for hitting at the top of the order, **Gleyber Torres** was ultimately squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-efficiency platoon advantages provided by **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.50) and **Bryce Harper** (62.31). Regarding risk management, we are keeping a close eye on **JJ Bleday**, whose score of 51.81 is heavily tethered to an unfavorable -14% dynamic platoon penalty against Houser. While he remains in the lineup due to his #3 order slot, he represents our lowest floor today; if the mid-game reports suggest an early hook or defensive substitution, we are prepared to pivot. We have confirmed **Tyler Freeman** remains in the minors with the Albuquerque Isotopes, so he remains firmly off the active board.",
